hostname - show or set the system name

SYNOPSIS
    hostname [name]

DESCRIPTION
    With no arguments, print the contents of /etc/hostname. If that file
    cannot be opened, print xv6. With a name, replace the file with that
    name and a newline. Changing the name requires root.

FILES
    /etc/hostname    Stored system name.

SEE ALSO
    login(1), sh(1)
